      "redistribution": "Permitted (public domain). FLAG FOR THE FOUNDER: the publisher asks that the data not be redistributed for a fee beyond reproduction costs; the open registry is free, but any paid tier that resells these parcel facts needs a reading of that clause. Attribution given anyway: MassGIS and the municipal assessing departments",
      "reviewed": "2026-11-03",
      "notes": "One zip per municipality, shapefile edition: shapefiles/l3parcels/L3_SHP_M###_NAME.zip in the public bucket download.massgis.digital.mass.gov, read through the S3 REST endpoint s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com (the website alias download.massgis.digital.mass.gov does not answer HTTPS). Each zip holds the Assess table as a dBase file (M###Assess_CY##_FY##.dbf, owner names included), a use-code lookup (M###UC_LUT), and the parcel shapefiles. These 350 files are every municipality except Boston, in MassGIS town-id order: the 176 towns of Middlesex (54), Worcester (60), Essex (34) and Norfolk (28) counties from Tier 2, and, from the statewide extension of 2026-11-03, the other 174 towns of the other ten counties, including Suffolk County's Chelsea, Revere and Winthrop (the bucket lists 351 towns, 934,157,232 bytes; the 350 here are 903 MB; Boston's file, 31 MB, is not listed because Boston is loaded from ma-boston-assessing and the adapter refuses it). Town files are refreshed on the towns' own schedules (the 2026-10-30 list shows dates from 2021 to 2026), so re-run discover/snapshot weekly and the collector keeps only changed files. Aggregate statewide geodatabases (L3_AGGREGATE_FGDB_*.zip, 7-8.5 GB) are NOT used. robots.txt: the S3 endpoint answers 403 AccessDenied to /robots.txt, which the collector reads as no rules; the mass.gov pages (terms_url, the MassGIS data page) answer the collector with 403 'Not allowed' and could not be read by it, so the licence text above was read from the metadata packed in the downloads themselves. Bucket listing used for discovery: https://s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/download.massgis.digital.mass.gov?list-type=2&prefix=shapefiles/l3parcels/L3_SHP_M . Landing page: the bucket's S3 listing for the l3parcels prefix (mass.gov answers the collector with 403, so its page cannot be the landing page); the town files are listed explicitly."
